  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x78BE" flags="0x0">
    <title>   VE TABLE - F29 - (SEE NOTES)</title>
    <description>F29&#013;&#010;BASE PULSE VOLUMETRIC EFFICIENCY VS RPM AND MAP&#013;&#010;TABLE VALUE = PERCENT*2.56&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Max value is 100%, anything over is ignored...&#013;&#010;VE is an added value.....F29 is vac only (open throttle), F29E is vac only (closed throttle), and F30 is based on rpm. So, for boosted conditions, F30 will be pulling a value based only on rpm and will be added to the &quot;100&quot; column in F29 for a total VE value. Fuel can be added in boost a number of ways, either by adding in the F29 table (up to 4k and affects ALL boost levels), in the F30 table (being a little more fine tuned with broader rpm range but still affects ALL boost levels), or in the F77 table (based on boost itself, but can tune for different levels of boost). In essence, VE works this way....F30 is always active, always using it&apos;s table as a lookup for VE and storing. Then it does a check for either open or closed throttle....if open, it uses a v</description>
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" />
      <units>Kpa</units>
      <indexcount>13</indexcount>
      <min>1000.000000</min>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="20" />
      <LABEL index="1" value="25" />
      <LABEL index="2" value="30" />
      <LABEL index="3" value="35" />
      <LABEL index="4" value="40" />
      <LABEL index="5" value="45" />
      <LABEL index="6" value="50" />
      <LABEL index="7" value="55" />
      <LABEL index="8" value="60" />
      <LABEL index="9" value="70" />
      <LABEL index="10" value="80" />
      <LABEL index="11" value="90" />
      <LABEL index="12" value="100" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" />
      <units>Rpm</units>
      <indexcount>10</indexcount>
      <min>1000.000000</min>
